<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>pain.001</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Messages</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">pain.001</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>pain.001 (CustomerCreditTransferInitiation)</strong> is the ISO 20022 message a corporate uses to instruct its bank to execute credit transfers; the current production version is <strong>pain.001.001.09</strong>. In hybrid format its <code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code> is capped at two occurrences — versions 3 and 9 allow up to 7 lines only in the legacy unstructured format, which ends on 15 November 2026.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How pain.001 works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>Corporates submit pain.001 via host-to-host files, SWIFT FileAct or banking portals. Because validation now happens at the point of entry, the ERP/TMS that generates the file must emit compliant addresses — there is no downstream repair. Vendor patches targeting pain.001 v9 hybrid output are a standard migration milestone.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 (pain.001 version constraints — CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex §0.31 / p5); Swift, Removal of unstructured address.3 / p1-1; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §24.4 / Appendix J.3.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
